Extracted from Pageborne commit 0d2bf71cb5ad244adae9184190a49893a0758401.
Third-party code, model and fixture licenses are included under vendor/stt and in built assets.

The built speech worker adapts Transformers.js 4.3.0 constructSessions to load
and release weight staging buffers serially. Its Apache-2.0 license is retained.
Source adaptation: scripts/serial-speech-sessions.mjs and src/speech-session-loader.js.

The optional three-model runtime includes sherpa-onnx v1.13.8
(commit 11afbd009a7f8c08f4bcf2fc1b265d0df4670fbf), ONNX Runtime 1.28.2,
kaldi-native-fbank 1.22.3 and linked third-party components. License texts are
under vendor/ensemble-runtime and vendor/stt. The adapter is built from
scripts/wasm with Emscripten 4.0.23; it contains no model weights.
The Conformer and Zipformer model distributions use Apache-2.0; Moonshine
uses the MIT license included in vendor/stt/moonshine-LICENSE. Downloads are
pinned by immutable revision, byte length and SHA-256 in ensemble-models.json.

Eigen source availability and the complete runtime notice inventory are in
vendor/ensemble-runtime/SOURCES.md. See docs/THIRD-PARTY.md for distribution scope.
